## 7. Sales orders, purchase orders, invoices, and vendor bills

- Keep invoicing easy. Prefer sensible defaults and nonblocking warnings over a wall of mandatory classifications.
- Customers should default to Due on Receipt / Immediate Payment unless a deliberate customer term overrides it.
- Sales orders should preserve product, revenue account, taxes, quantities, pricing, customer, and downstream invoice linkage.
- Purchase orders should preserve vendor, vendor reference, taxes, product/expense/inventory account routing, receipt/bill linkage, and company.
- Vendor bills must show the vendor and allow `Auto-Complete` / purchase-document linkage when the vendor and company match eligible POs.
- A prior view regression hid vendor/PO fields on vendor bills. When editing invoice/payment views, regression-test customer invoices, vendor bills, receipts, refunds, and all companies.
- Do not allow Stripe fee/payment-type UI logic to affect vendor bills or purchase-document lookup.
- Broad accounting guardrails previously blocked PO confirmation for missing taxes and periodic-valuation expense configuration. The user asked not to remove everything after initially objecting, but the desired direction is lightweight assistance without breaking ordinary purchasing.

## 8. Accounting and cash flow

- Main concern has been cash-flow pressure from service growth, receivables timing, and funding the operating cycle—not merely reported profitability.
- Focus analyses on actual bank transactions, A/R aging, collections timing, service WIP, inventory purchases, payroll, taxes, equipment/fuel spend, and Stripe settlement timing.
- Do not "clean up" or reconcile by guessing. Match evidence, preserve audit trails, and keep unresolved items visible.
- Expense account additions requested for vehicle fuel, equipment fuel, and shop tools. Verify the final chart-of-accounts names and codes before using them.
- Mississippi sales/payroll tax mappings have required attention. Tax advice and filings are high-stakes; validate authoritative rules and accountant approval.
- Stripe reconciliation should separately record gross customer receipt, processing-fee income charged to the customer, actual Stripe fee expense, clearing movement, and net bank settlement.

